xes for the latest Windows builds\"],\"system_requirements\":{\"minimum\":{\"os\":\"Windows 7 or later\",\"processor\":null,\"ram\":null,\"disk_space\":null,\"graphics\":null},\"recommended\":{\"os\":\"Windows 10 or later\",\"processor\":null,\"ram\":null,\"disk_space\":null},\"_note\":\"Detailed hardware specifications are not published by the developer.\"},\"faqs\":[{\"question\":\"Is Autorun Organizer free to use?\",\"answer\":\"Yes, Autorun Organizer is distributed as freeware, meaning it is free to download and use on Windows without a subscription or trial period.\"},{\"question\":\"Will disabling startup items harm my system?\",\"answer\":\"Disabling third-party autostart items is safe and reversible through the program. Windows core services are clearly marked so you can avoid disabling anything essential.\"},{\"question\":\"Can Autorun Organizer stop programs from re-enabling themselves?\",\"answer\":\"Yes, its automatic monitoring feature watches for stubborn applications that try to reactivate after an update and blocks those reactivation attempts automatically.\"}],\"installation_guide\":{\"steps\":[\"Step 1: Click the download button to grab the Autorun Organizer installer for Windows.\",\"Step 2: Locate the downloaded setup file and double-click it to launch the installation wizard.\",\"Step 3: Follow the on-screen prompts to complete installation, then launch the program to review your startup list.\"],\"compatibility_notes\":\"Compatible with Windows 7, 8, 10, and 11, both 32-bit and 64-bit editions.\",\"common_issues\":[\"Issue: Installer won't launch → Solution: Right-click the setup file and choose Run as administrator.\",\"Issue: Disabled app reappears after reboot → Solution: Check the auto-monitoring log to confirm the entry was blocked by the watcher.\"]},\"tags\":[\"startupmanager\",\"freeware\",\"bootoptimizer\"],\"_tags_note\":\"3 single-token tags describing subtype and license.\",\"software_type\":\"SIMPLE_UTILITY\",\"moat_data\":{}}","re