\"Portable\" versions (often for Windows and macOS). If they exist on the official site or trusted repositories (GitHub\/PortableApps), extract their URLs and variants explicitly.\n\n3. **FAQ GENERATION**:\n- Generate 0-3 FAQs based on genuine user demand. Zero FAQs is acceptable for simple utilities where no real questions exist. Quality over quantity \u2014 2 excellent FAQs beat 3 padded ones. RANDOMIZE: if the software has rich FAQ material, generate 2-3; if it's a simple tool, simply omit it.\n- If the source doesn't contain FAQs, create them based on common user questions for this type of software (e.g., \"Is [Software] free?\", \"Is it safe to download?\", \"What are the system requirements?\").\n- **SIMPLE_UTILITY FAQ RULE**: If software_type is SIMPLE_UTILITY, the faqs array MUST be empty []. Do NOT generate any FAQ content for simple utilities \u2014 not even one. This is a hard exclusion, not a suggestion.\n- Ensure answers are VERSION-AGNOSTIC and journal-style. Write FAQs about the software in general (e.g., \"Is Malwarebytes free?\" NOT \"Is Malwarebytes 5.5.5.253 free?\"). These FAQs persist across version updates and must remain accurate regardless of version. Never embed specific version numbers in FAQ questions or answers.\n\n7. DOWNLOAD LINKS: Extract all download links verbatim from the context. The system already handles referral link filtering and de-obfuscation; simply extract the URLs precisely as they appear in the source text. Whitelist GitHub, SourceForge, and Official App Stores.\n8. FILE SIZE: Be aggressive in finding the file size. If not in the context, SEARCH for it. Extract it precisely.\n9. DEVELOPER: Identify the developer. If not in the text, YOU MUST SEARCH for the official vendor. Do NOT leave null.\n\n10. **MOAT SECTION**:\n- `moat_data` is MANDATORY for every article. You MUST always include the key in your JSON response.\n- **SIMPLE_UTILITY MOAT RULE**: If software_type is SIMPLE_UTILITY, set moat_data to `{}` (empty object). Do NOT generate any moat content \u2014 no headings, no recipes, no why text. This is a hard exclusion.\n- For COMPLEX_ENGINE software: If the provided context does not contain \"Quick Start\" or \"Settings\" guides, YOU MUST SEARCH for \"[software name] settings\", \"[software name] tips\", \"[software name] quick start guide\".\n- For COMPLEX_ENGINE software: Generate 2-3 practical settings recipes or quick-start steps that deliver real user value. NEVER pad with generic steps.\n\n4. WRITING STYLE:\n- YOU MUST FOLLOW THE EXACT SAME \"HUMAN WRITING STYLE\" (Sentence Variance, No Robotic Vocab, Syntax Variety) as defined for the regular mode.\n- The site voice must remain consistent across all posts.\n\n5. TAXONOMY:\n- Map the detected software to the `VALID_TAXONOMY_MAP` slugs.\n- FORMULA: You MUST select MULTIPLE categories. First, choose the supported Operating Systems. Then, choose the Software Type. Use SEARCH to verify categorization if unsure.\n\n6. CATEGORIZATION:\n- `category`: Return a comma-separated list of the selected category slugs.\n10. **FILE SIZE RULE**:\n- You MUST return only a single, clean value for `file_size` (e.g., '15.5 MB').\n- If multiple installers or platforms exist, pick the primary Windows installer size.\n- NEVER list multiple sizes or add parenthetical descriptions like '(online installer)' in the size field.\n\nHYBRID MODE: You have been provided with rich source content. Use it as your PRIMARY source for article structure, version data, and download links. Use Google Search ONLY for: (1) missing metadata like Developer, File Size, License, (2) the moat_data section \u2014 you MUST search for \"[software name] tips\", \"[software name] settings guide\", \"[software name] quick start\" to generate moat_data. Do NOT use search to find a different version than what is in the provided content.\n\nSTATE: PARTIAL REGENERATION. Only regenerate the specific sections requested. Leave all other sections unchanged.\n\nCONTEXT \/ ARTICLE DATA:\nSource Context:\nOpera Air is a brand new browser with mindfulness at its core, that meets the needs of our busy lives by reducing distractions and helping you focus. It integrates features that support relaxation and well-being, such as meditation and breathing practices, binaural beats, and neck stretches.\nDeveloped with tried and true methods, Opera Air creates an environment that helps boost productivity and creativity while promoting mental health and creating a calmer, more focused browsing experience. It\u2019s mission is to help people feel better by turning everyday browsing into a powerful tool for stress relief and improved focus.\nOpera Air comes with Aria, a built-in AI and browser assistant. Enjoy AI chat, text and image generation, webpage summaries, voice output and more \u2013 no subscription or sign-up required.\nElevate Your Browsing Experience\nIn the digital age, a fast browser that prioritizes your security and privacy is essential for efficient web navigation. Enter the Opera Air Browser \u2013 an innovative and robust web browser designed to transform the way you explore the internet. With its sleek interface, advanced features, and top-notch security, this browser stands out as the ultimate choice for internet users seeking an unparalleled browsing experience.\nLightning-Fast Performance\nSpeed is paramount when it comes to browsing the web, and Opera Air Browser excels in this regard. Built with cutting-edge technology, this fast browser ensures lightning-fast page load times, enabling you to access your favorite websites and online content without delays. Say goodbye to frustrating lags and buffering \u2013 Opera Air Browser\u2019s optimized performance guarantees smooth and seamless navigation.\nEnhanced Security and Privacy Protection\nYour online security and privacy are of utmost importance, and Opera Air Browser is committed to safeguarding your digital footprint. Equipped with advanced security protocols, this secure browser protects you from cyber threats, malware, and phishing attacks. Additionally, the Browser features robust Privacy Protection settings, including built-in ad-blockers and tracking protection, ensuring that your personal information remains confidential and your browsing activities stay private.\nIntuitive User Interface\nNavigating the internet should be a hassle-free experience, and Opera Air Browser delivers just that. Its intuitive user interface is designed with simplicity and functionality in mind. Whether you\u2019re a tech-savvy individual or a casual internet user, you\u2019ll find Opera Air Browser\u2019s layout easy to navigate. Customizable options allow you to tailor the browser to your preferences, enhancing your overall browsing experience.\nSeamless Cross-Device Syncing\nIn today\u2019s multi-device world, staying connected across various platforms is crucial. This Browser offers seamless cross-device syncing, allowing you to access your bookmarks, browsing history, and saved passwords from any device. Whether you\u2019re using a smartphone, tablet, or desktop, Opera Air Browser ensures a consistent and synchronized experience, making it easy to pick up where you left off.\nRich Customization Options\nOpera Air Browser believes in giving users the power to personalize their browsing environment. With a plethora of customization options, you can change themes, add extensions, and organize your tabs to suit your preferences. Whether you prefer a minimalist look or a feature-rich setup, Opera Air Browser offers the flexibility to create a browsing environment that aligns with your unique style.\nInnovative Features\nOpera Air Browser is packed with innovative features that enhance your online experience. The built-in screenshot tool allows you to capture and share web content effortlessly, while the integrated search functionality ensures quick access to information. Additionally, the browser\u2019s reader mode provides a distraction-free reading experience by