[2026-09-04 17:29:57] [INFO] DEBUG: Moat Data Structure {"moat":{"quick_start_recipes":[{"title":"Setting Up Your First DVB Device","description":"Launch ProgDVB and navigate to Settings > Device Manager. Select your DVB card from the detected hardware list. Configure the tuner type (DVB-S\/S2, DVB-C, DVB-T, ATSC, or ISDB-T) based on your broadcast source. Set the LNB frequency if using satellite, or input your cable provider details for DVB-C connections. Click 'Apply' and then run a channel scan to populate your channel list."},{"title":"Configuring XMLTV EPG Guide","description":"Open Settings > EPG and select 'XmlTV' as your guide source. Download or subscribe to an XMLTV provider such as epg.one. Point ProgDVB to your XMLTV file location and set the update interval. Map the XMLTV channel IDs to your ProgDVB channels using the Channel Editor. The guide will now populate automatically with program schedules."},{"title":"Recording and Timeshifting Setup","description":"Allocate a dedicated storage folder for recordings via Settings > Recording. Enable timeshifting and configure your buffer size (unlimited disk or RAM-based). To record, press the record button or set scheduled recordings in the EPG. Recordings can be saved in MKV or MP4 format. Enable picture-in-picture to watch one channel while browsing or recording another."}]}}
