ems explicitly documented in official changelog for THIS version\". I need to know which version is \"THIS\". Given the confusion, I'll use the detected_version 7.71.0 or the metadata 7.72.7. I'll probably go with 7.71.0 since the changelog explicitly has it. But the download links are for 7.72.7. I'll check the context: it has \"&lt;h3&gt;Changes in version 7.71.0:&lt;/h3&gt;\" and then list. So the latest explicit version in context is 7.71.0. I'll use that for whats_new. I'll extract the items under 7.71.0. But there are also earlier versions. I'll only include the most recent version's changes, or maybe all? The rule says \"up to a maximum of 8 bullet points.\" I'll take the changes from 7.71.0 and maybe 7.70.7 if needed. I'll be concise.\n\n   - System requirements: The context has \"Minimum hardware requirements:\" with details. I'll extract those. OS: \"Windows 7. 8, 8.1, 10 (32-bit and 64-bit)\". Processor: \"Intel Pentium III Processor 500 MHz or better for SD channels. Intel Pentium 4 Processor 4.0 GHz or better for HD channels.\" RAM: \"512 MB memory on board.\" Disk space: \"50 MB of disk space (plus the space required for Video&Audio Recording).\" Graphics: \"SVGA Videocard Adapter with 32 MB onboard memory.\" I'll format system_requirements minimum accordingly.\n\n   - OS support: From context: \"Supported Operating Systems: Windows 7. 8, 8.1, 10 (32-bit and 64-bit)\". So os_support: \"Windows 7, 8, 8.1, 10\". But also maybe newer? The download links are for Windows only. I'll stick to what's in context.\n\n   - Language support: The context doesn't explicitly mention languages, but it mentions \"Skins for OSD and GUI\" and \"Interface Language Localizations\". I'll set language_support as \"English, multiple languages (localizations)\" or just \"English\". The rule: \"language_support: 'English, Spanish, French (multi-language)'\". I'll see if the context mentions specific languages. It doesn't. I'll set as \"English, multi-language support\" but need