value but update technical data (version, links). You MUST generate ALL top-level SEO fields (title, meta_description, focus_keyword, slug) \u2014 they are required for the new plugin-standard post.\n\nCONTEXT \/ ARTICLE DATA:\nSource Context:\nWine is open source software that allows users of Unix-based systems (such as Linux and macOS) to run applications originally developed for Microsoft Windows.\n\nWhat exactly is Wine?\n\nContrary to popular belief, Wine is not an emulator. Its name is actually a recursive acronym:\n\n\nWine Is Not an Eemulator\n\n\nRather than simulating an entire computer configuration or operating system, Wine acts as a compatibility layer. It translates program requests (Windows API calls) into commands that the Linux kernel can understand in real time.\n\nKey benefits\n\n1. High productivity\n\nBecause there's no heavy hardware emulation, apps often run at near-native speeds. In some specific cases (due to more efficient memory management in Linux) certain programs may even run faster.\n\n2. Independence and security\n\nWine is built on clean code independent of Microsoft. This allows users to benefit from:\n\n\nLinux security: Protects the system from typical Windows viruses.\n\n\n\nCore stability: Fewer system crashes when working with critical software.\n\n\n3. Flexibility of libraries\n\nAlthough independent, Wine can use Microsoft's original dynamic libraries (.dll) if this is necessary for the correct operation of a specific application.\n\nWho is it suitable for?\n\nWine is ideal for:\n\n\nGamers: Through projects like Proton (based on Wine), thousands of Windows games run flawlessly on Steam under Linux.\n\n\n\nProfessionals: Allows the use of specific design or engineering tools that do not have a Linux version.\n\n\n\nNew users: It facilitates migration from Windows to Linux, removing the barrier of missing software.\n\n\nWine continues to be one of the most important projects in the free software world, making operating systems more open and interoperable.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOfficial page | ChangesDownload: Wine 11.0 Stable (31.6 MB)\n\nDownload: Wine 11.17 Beta (44.6 MB)\n\nSOURCE_URL: unknown\n\nPHP_DETECTED_METADATA (Weak Hints):\n{\"software_name\":\"Wine\",\"version\":\"11.17 Beta\",\"homepage\":\"https:\\\/\\\/www.winehq.org\\\/\",\"category\":\"\",\"is_existing_article\":true,\"detected_version\":\"\",\"detected_file_size\":\"31.6 MB\",\"resolved_links\":[{\"url\":\"https:\\\/\\\/dl.winehq.org\\\/wine\\\/source\\\/11.x\\\/wine-11.17.tar.xz\",\"normalized_url\":\"https:\\\/\\\/dl.winehq.org\\\/wine\\\/source\\\/11.x\\\/wine-11.17.tar.xz\",\"text\":\"Wine 11.17 Beta\",\"context\":\"Download: Wine 11.17 Beta (44.6 MB)\",\"source\":\"anchor\",\"source_host\":\"dl.winehq.org\",\"platform\":\"Linux\",\"variant\":\"Beta\",\"link_type\":\"portal\",\"confidence\":1,\"is_primary\":false,\"approved\":true,\"rejected_reason\":\"\"}],\"detected_links\":[{\"url\":\"https:\\\/\\\/dl.winehq.org\\\/wine\\\/source\\\/11.x\\\/wine-11.17.tar.xz\",\"normalized_url\":\"https:\\\/\\\/dl.winehq.org\\\/wine\\\/source\\\/11.x\\\/wine-11.17.tar.xz\",\"text\":\"Wine 11.17 Beta\",\"context\":\"Download: Wine 11.17 Beta (44.6 MB)\",\"source\":\"anchor\",\"source_host\":\"dl.winehq.org\",\"platform\":\"Linux\",\"variant\":\"Beta\",\"link_type\":\"portal\",\"confidence\":1,\"is_primary\":false,\"approved\":true,\"rejected_reason\":\"\"}],\"detected_trial\":\"\",\"detected_direct\":\"\",\"detected_portal\":\"\",\"grounding_hints\":[]}\n\nVALID_TAXONOMY_MAP:\n[]\n\nSTRICT IDENTITY RULE (DISCOVERY MODE):\n- If the Software Name or Version in the CONTEXT below differs from the Metadata above, the CONTEXT is the absolute source of truth.\n- Use the name and version found in the Context HTML for all schema fields.\n\n**DOWNLOAD LINKS**: Do NOT generate download_section or download links. The system will populate download links from verified source data. Focus on article content only.\n- TRUSTED SOURCES: github.com,