em. Wait, the schema includes: needs_manual_input, tech_specs, whats_new, system_requirements, tags, hero_section. No \"introduction\" or \"features\" or \"faqs\" or \"pros_cons\" etc. But the earlier part of the prompt describes a different schema? Let's check: The prompt says \"JSON SCHEMA:\" and then provides a specific schema. That schema includes: needs_manual_input, tech_specs, whats_new, system_requirements, tags, hero_section. It does NOT include faqs, pros_cons, installation_guide, moat_data, competitors, tags (wait, tags is there). Actually, the prompt starts with \"You are a professional software documentation writer. Use web search to find accurate, up-to-date information about the software. You are a strict JSON content generator. Return ONLY one valid JSON object with no markdown formatting and no code fences.\" Then it lists a lot of rules, including moat_data, competitors, tags, etc. But then it says \"JSON SCHEMA:\" and provides a specific schema. The schema seems to be the definitive output format. The earlier rules about faqs, moat_data, etc., might be from a different mode or the user is combining instructions. But the final \"JSON SCHEMA:\" section seems to override or specify exactly what to output.\n\n   Let's read carefully: The prompt has two big parts. Part 1: \"You are a professional software documentation writer...\" with many rules about faqs, moat_data, competitors, tags, etc. Part 2: \"STRICT IDENTITY RULE (DISCOVERY MODE)...\" and then \"JSON SCHEMA:\" with a specific structure. And then \"STATE: PARTIAL REGENERATION.\" Maybe the user wants me to output the JSON schema based on the context, following the rules in Part 1, but the output must conform to the schema in Part 2.\n\n   Let's examine the JSON SCHEMA provided:\n   ```json\n   {\n       \"needs_manual_input\": [\n           \"tech_specs.homepage\",\n           \"system_requirements.minimum.os\"\n       ],\n       \"tech_specs\": {\n           \"software_name\": \"Full name\",\n           \"file_name\": \"setup.exe or null if unknown\",\n           \"version\": \"string or null - ONLY from official site, never guess\",\n           \"license\": \"Free/Trial/Paid\",\n           \"developer\": \"Company name (MUST extract)\",\n           \"homepage\": \"URL\",\n           \"changelogurl\": \"URL or null - ONLY from official site\",\n           \"file_size\": \"string or null - ONLY if clearly shown on official page. If multiple sizes exist, pick the primary Windows size.\",\n           \"os_support\": \"Comma-separated list of ALL supported platforms (e.g., Windows 11, 10; macOS 12+; Linux). MUST extract.\",\n           \"language_support\": \"English, Spanish, French (multi-language)\",\n           \"last_updated\": \"string or null - ONLY if explicitly dated. If active but date missing, use current Month YYYY.\"\n       },\n       \"whats_new\": [\n           \"ONLY items explicitly documented in official changelog for THIS version\",\n           \"If vendor says 'bug fixes and improvements', use that exact phrase\",\n           \"Make the changelog concise, short, and include only the most important points, up to a maximum of 8 bullet points.\",\n           \"Empty array [] if no changelog found - do NOT invent features\"\n       ],\n       \"system_requirements\": {\n           \"minimum\": {\n               \"os\": \"string or null - only if explicitly stated\",\n               \"processor\": \"string or null - only if explicitly stated\",\n               \"ram\": \"string or null - NEVER assume '4 GB' unless written\",\n               \"disk_space\": \"string or null - NEVER assume '500 MB' unless written\",\n               \"graphics\": \"string or null - only if explicitly stated\"\n           },\n           \"recommended\": {\n               \"os\": \"string or null\",\n               \"processor\": \"string or null\",\n               \"ram\": \"string or null\",\n               \"disk_space\": \"string or null\"\n           },\n    